Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:14:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation: names of the execution options reserved

The execution options are read by mfem_mgis::initialize from the arguments of the program, before the initialization of MPI, whatever the options declared by the program: a program must not use their long or short names for its own options.
---
 docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst b/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
index 202379ee9a..466f3facc4 100644
--- a/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
+++ b/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
@@ -475,6 +475,12 @@ choice:
   solvers and memory of hypre) and :code:`--post-processings`
   (:code:`-ppd`). These options are refused in the other modes.
 
+These options are read by :code:`mfem_mgis::initialize` directly from the
+arguments of the program, before the initialization of :code:`MPI` and of
+:code:`hypre`, whatever the options declared by the program: a program must
+not use their long or short names (:code:`-x`, :code:`-fe`, :code:`-bh`,
+:code:`-lsd`, :code:`-ppd`) for its own options.
+
 The 16 combinations of the mixed mode are tested
 (:code:`ExecutionSettingsTest`, when the behaviour library for the GPU is
 built). The settings give:
